-- #948 (S1 crash + S0 silent wrongness): a CROSS-MODULE impl that overrides NONE of
-- an interface's methods — every one inherited from an interface DEFAULT — lowers to
-- ZERO `CImplEntry`, because `lowerDeclImpl` projects a `DImpl` to one entry per
-- method it DEFINES.  (Same-module the question never arises: desugar's
-- `fillImplDefaults` specializes the default INTO the impl, which is a real, tagged
-- entry.)  The native emitter derived "the type tags this interface's dict can carry"
-- from those entries, so such an impl was invisible to it, in two ways:
--
--   Speak/Dog — Dog is the interface's ONLY impl, so `ifaceTags Speak` was EMPTY and
--     the runtime dispatcher `@mdk_disp_speak_0_1` was emitted with no arm at all,
--     just `unreachable`.  The dict-routed call inside `useSpeak` ran it → SIGSEGV
--     (exit 139), on a program `check` greens and `medaka run` prints correctly.
--
--   Loud/Cat+Dog — Cat OVERRIDES `loud`, Dog inherits it.  `loud` then had exactly
--     one tagged impl, so the `soleImplDirect` shortcut compiled every dict-routed
--     call — including `useLoud Dog` — into a direct call to Cat's `@mdk_impl_Cat_loud`.
--     No crash: `useLoud Dog` just returned "MEOW".  Silent wrongness.
--
-- Both halves need the CONSTRAINED FORWARDER (`useSpeak`/`useLoud`): a direct
-- `speak Dog` in `main` resolves RKey and takes emitDefaultRKey, which was always
-- correct (see the sibling default_method_numlit_crossmodule fixture, whose call IS
-- direct — which is exactly why it never caught this).
--
-- Must print woof / MEOW / WOOF.  A crash is the Speak half regressing; a second
-- "MEOW" on the last line is the Loud half regressing.
import dface.{Speak(..), speak, Loud(..), loud}

data Cat = Cat
data Dog = Dog

-- INHERITS `speak`: an impl with an entirely empty body.
impl Speak Dog where


impl Loud Cat where
  loud _ = "MEOW"

-- INHERITS `loud`, alongside Cat's override.
impl Loud Dog where


useSpeak : Speak a => a -> String
useSpeak x = speak x

useLoud : Loud a => a -> String
useLoud x = loud x

main : <IO> Unit
main =
  let _ = putStrLn (useSpeak Dog)
  let _ = putStrLn (useLoud Cat)
  putStrLn (useLoud Dog)
